    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7063": {
      "title": "Content Producer",
      "description": "Content Producer - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Content Producer Wollongong, NSW, Australia (Hybrid) Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role As Content Producer, you will create clear, compelling and on-brand content across UOW’s marketing channels and campaigns. Working in the Creative Production team, you will produce written, editorial, social and multimedia content to brief, contribute practical ideas to campaign and editorial planning, and help tell stories that support recruitment, reputation and the University’s strategic narrative. In this role, you will: Produce high-quality content across formats, including copywriting, editorial, social, video, photography and multimedia. Generate and pitch proactive content ideas, identifying stories, trends and always-on content opportunities that engage audiences. Contribute to editorial and campaign planning, advising on format, treatment, audience and channel approach. Work with cross-functional marketing squads to deliver integrated campaigns and content initiatives. Apply audience, channel and performance insight to improve content quality and impact. Use brand, editorial and accessibility standards consistently, with curiosity about emerging content trends, tools and responsible AI-enabled practice. About the Team The Brand and Marketing Division shapes how UOW is understood, chosen and championed by students, partners and communities. The Creative Production team operates as the Division’s in-house studio, producing content and design for campaigns, channels and priority initiatives. You will work within a squad-based delivery model, taking direction from the Senior Manager, Creative Production and working closely with the Lead Content Producer, who leads editorial planning and craft standards for the studio. The Division is evolving how it partners with faculties and portfolios, strengthens brand and reputation, and delivers high-quality marketing outcomes. This is a practical, hands-on role in that model: making good content, bringing useful ideas, and helping the work land well. What You’ll Bring A degree in a relevant discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and training. Experience producing content across multiple formats, such as copy, social media, editorial, video or multimedia, in a marketing, communications or creative environment. Strong writing, editing or multimedia production skills, with the ability to produce clear, accessible and on-brand content to brief. The ability to identify good stories, generate practical content ideas and shape them for different audiences and channels. Curiosity about audience insight, content performance, emerging trends, production tools and responsible AI-enabled practice. Good organisational skills and the ability to manage concurrent work to deadlines in a high-volume production environment. Strong collaboration skills, including the ability to work in a team or squad, take direction and respond well to feedback. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Permanent/Continuing | Full-time Level 5: $85,682 - $96,898 + 17% Superannuation Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus / Hybrid Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a resume, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Lorna Farrar, Chief Communications & Marketing Officer via email lfarrar@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Wednesday 21 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7063 Job Category Marketing, Communications & Advancement Posting Date 10/07/2026, 05:59 PM Apply Before 10/21/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU (Hybrid) Similar Jobs Lead Content Producer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Posted on 10/07/2026 Lead the planning and creation of written, editorial, video, audio and multimedia content that brings the University’s brand, campaigns and stories to life across channels. See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Content Producer - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
