    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7051": {
      "title": "Technical Coordinator, Visual Arts",
      "description": "Technical Coordinator, Visual Arts - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Technical Coordinator, Visual Arts Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose ‑ driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Technical Services Coordinator plays a pivotal role in ensuring the effective delivery of technical services within the School of Creative Arts & Humanities. Reporting to the School Operations Manager, this position coordinates technical operations, workplace health and safety, technical staff deployment, communications, and systems management to support the school's teaching, learning and research activities. Working across various visual arts disciplines you will be a key link between academic staff and the technical services team, helping create exceptional experiences for students and staff. Key responsibilities: Coordinate and supervise technical services operations to support learning, teaching and research activities. Lead and support Technical Services Officers through workload planning, recruitment, onboarding and day-to-day supervision. Coordinate the procurement, maintenance and lifecycle management of technical equipment, facilities and resources. Drive workplace health and safety compliance, training, inductions and risk management activities across School facilities. Build strong working relationships with academic, professional and external stakeholders to support school operations, events and continuous improvement initiatives. About the Team The School of Creative Arts & Humanities sits within the Faculty of Arts, Society and Business, a faculty committed to empowering the next generation to think critically, act creatively and engage globally. The school delivers transformative educational experiences that foster curiosity, artistic excellence and interdisciplinary collaboration. This role works closely with academic and professional staff and leads a dedicated technical services team that enables outstanding teaching, research and creative practice outcomes. What You’ll Bring A bachelor's degree and/or extensive relevant experience with specialist expertise in a related field. Demonstrated experience leading, coordinating and developing staff within a collaborative team environment. Strong knowledge of workplace health and safety requirements, particularly within teaching, research or creative environments. Proven ability to implement and improve operational processes, procedures and service delivery outcomes. Excellent communication, stakeholder engagement and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and take responsibility for outcomes. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Permanent/Continuing | Full-time Level 6/7: $96,898 - $119,986 + 17% Superannuation Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Tim Beniuk, School Operations Manager, Creative Arts and Humanities on tbeniuk@uow.edu.au or + 61 2 4298 1210. Closing Date: Thursday 29 October  2026 , 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Woll