    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6835": {
      "title": "Partnership Specialist, Agreements & Visits",
      "description": "Partnership Specialist, Agreements & Visits - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Partnership Specialist, Agreements & Visits Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose‑driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role An exciting opportunity exists for an experienced partnerships and stakeholder engagement professional to join UOW's Global Partnership team as a Partnership Specialist, Agreements & Visits. Working at the centre of the University's international engagement activities, you will play a pivotal role in managing institutional international agreements, supporting strategic global partnerships, and coordinating high-profile international delegations and visits. This is a varied and highly visible role that combines relationship management, compliance, project coordination and operational leadership to support UOW's global strategy. Key responsibilities: Manage the development, execution and ongoing administration of international partnership agreements and associated legal documentation. Coordinate inbound international delegations and visits, ensuring a professional and impactful experience for stakeholders and visitors. Develop and maintain effective partnership management processes that support compliance and operational excellence. Prepare executive briefings, reports and partnership documentation for senior leaders and key stakeholders. Oversee foreign arrangements reporting requirements and maintain accurate institutional records and partnership data About the Team The role sits within Global Partnerships and supports the University's Strategic Partnerships and Mobility function. Working closely with faculties, Legal Services, the Vice-Chancellor's Office, Government and Community Relations, and international partners, the team drives the development and management of UOW's global partnerships and engagement activities. This is a collaborative and outward-facing team that contributes directly to the University's international strategy and global reputation. What You’ll Bring Degree qualification or equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Demonstrated experience managing complex partnerships, agreements, MOUs or similar contractual arrangements. Proven ability to coordinate high-level visits, events, delegations or stakeholder engagement activities. Exceptional communication and relationship management skills, with experience engaging senior executives and diverse stakeholders. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities, analyse information and maintain a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Continuing | Full-time Level 6/7 | $96,898 - $119,986 plus 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a CV, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Brooke Dixon, Manager Strategic Partnerships and Mobility at brookew@uow.edu.au Closing Date: 1 November 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is comm