    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7037": {
      "title": "Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Compliance Officer - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Compliance Officer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Compliance Officer will play a key role in supporting the delivery of UOW's Risk and Compliance Management Uplift Program. Working across the University, you will help coordinate strategic initiatives that strengthen risk management capability, compliance maturity, organisational resilience and risk culture. This is an exciting opportunity for a project professional who enjoys driving change, engaging stakeholders and contributing to meaningful organisational improvement. Key responsibilities: Coordinate the delivery of enterprise risk and compliance uplift initiatives, ensuring milestones, deliverables and implementation activities are effectively managed. Support capability development through training programs, workshops, communication campaigns and organisational change initiatives. Facilitate stakeholder engagement and consultation activities across faculties, divisions and controlled entities to support successful program outcomes. Prepare project reporting, governance documentation, presentations and implementation updates to support effective oversight and decision making. About the Team The position sits within the Integrity, Legal and Governance Division in the Vice-President Operations Portfolio and forms part of the Risk, Compliance and Assurance team. The team works collaboratively across the University to strengthen governance, risk management, compliance and assurance practices. The team is currently delivering strategic initiatives that enhance organisational resilience and support informed decision-making across UOW. What You'll Bring A degree in project management, business, risk management, governance, compliance, organisational development or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience coordinating projects, programs or organisational improvement initiatives in a complex environment. Experience supporting change management, capability development, stakeholder engagement, training or communication programs. Strong organisational , analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and multiple workstreams. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare reports, presentations and governance documentation. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Fixed term | Full-time appointment (15 months) Level 5: $85,682 - $96,898 + 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available This position is not suitable for remote working arrangements. Must hold and maintain a valid, current Australian Drivers Licence Position Description How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be requested to submit a resume and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Senior Manager, Compliance Joel McLean joelm@uow.edu.au The successful candidate will be required to undertake a National Criminal History Check. Closing Date: Wednesday 25 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committe