    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/6991": {
      "title": "Fire and HVAC Supervisor",
      "description": "Fire and HVAC Supervisor - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Fire and HVAC Supervisor Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Fire & HVAC Supervisor Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Fire & HVAC Supervisor provides specialist technical leadership and operational oversight of UOW’s critical fire protection and HVAC systems. With fire services as the primary focus, you will ensure these essential assets are safe, reliable, compliant and effectively managed throughout their lifecycle, while providing supporting oversight of HVAC systems across the University. Key responsibilities: Provide specialist technical leadership for the operation, maintenance, compliance and performance of fire protection systems, with supporting oversight of UOW’s HVAC portfolio. Oversee asset lifecycle planning, preventative and corrective maintenance, condition assessments, reliability improvement and renewal planning for fire and HVAC assets. Manage statutory inspections, testing, certification, compliance audits and defect rectification, ensuring risks and non-conformances are appropriately addressed. Manage specialist contractors, service agreements, emergency response arrangements, expenditure and performance, while providing technical input into capital works and infrastructure renewal projects. About the Team The role sits within UOW’s Infrastructure and Property Division (IPD) and reports to the Maintenance Manager. IPD is responsible for the provision and care of the University’s campuses, delivering and maintaining safe, sustainable and high-quality environments that support learning, teaching, research and the wider University community. You will work closely with University stakeholders, specialist contractors, consultants, certifiers, regulatory bodies and external authorities across UOW’s Wollongong, Innovation and Liverpool campuses. What You’ll Bring We are looking for an experienced building services professional with strong technical knowledge of fire systems and the ability to manage critical assets, contractors and compliance obligations in a complex operational environment. A relevant trade qualification and/or a minimum of five years’ experience maintaining fire systems and/or associated HVAC mechanical systems. Demonstrated knowledge of AFSS requirements, AS 1851 and the statutory compliance framework applicable to fire systems. Strong applied understanding of building services, including fire, mechanical, hydraulic and electrical systems, together with an understanding of HVAC Systems Demonstrated experience managing specialist contractors, maintenance programs, asset lifecycle planning, reliability and regulatory compliance. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication, contract administration, budget management and risk management capabilities. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Permanent/Continuing, Full-time appointment Level 6/7: $96,898 - $119,986 + 17% superannuation commensurate with experience and capability Location: Wollongong Campus, with work across Innovation and Liverpool campuses as required. This position is campus-based and is not suitable for remote working arrangements. The position requires participation in after-hours and on-call arrangements as required. A current Australian Driver Licence is required. The successful candidate will be required to obtain and maintain a Working with Children Check Clearance and satisfactorily complete a National Criminal Check. Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a resume and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Maintenance Manager, Nathan Barlow on nbarlow@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Tuesday 27 October 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 6991 Job Category Facilities Management Posting Date 10/12/2026, 04:17 PM Apply Before 10/27/2026, 05:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Cont