      "title": "People Advisor",
      "description": "People Advisor - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs People Advisor Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked among the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The People Advisor is the first point of contact for managers and staff on a broad range of employee lifecycle matters. Working within the People & Culture team, you'll provide timely, accurate and solutions-focused advice while helping to ensure compliance with university policies, Enterprise Agreements and industrial obligations. You'll work closely with People Partners and broader People & Culture teams to deliver responsive, people-centred services across the University. Key responsibilities: Provide trusted advice and support to managers and staff across the employee lifecycle. Support staffing activities including onboarding, probation, performance management and organisational change. Assist with position management processes including position descriptions, reclassifications, extensions and promotions. Interpret and apply HR policies, Enterprise Agreements and industrial obligations. Coach managers on best practice people management and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives. About the Team The People & Culture division is dedicated to empowering our people and enhancing the employee experience across UOW. Working within the People Partnering function, you'll collaborate with People Partners, Shared Services and specialist P&C teams to deliver high-quality advice and support. Together, we provide responsive, innovative and people-centred services that help our university community thrive. What You'll Bring Relevant tertiary qualifications or equivalent professional experience in Human Resources or a related field. Experience providing practical, solutions-focused HR advice across employee lifecycle matters. Knowledge of HR policies, Enterprise Agreements and industrial obligations. Strong stakeholder management skills with the ability to build trusted relationships and influence outcomes. Demonstrated ability to support managers and contribute to efficient, customer-focused HR service delivery. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility. Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies. Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period. Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year. Ongoing professional development and career progression opportunities. Role Details Employment Type: Fixed-term, part-time (0.4 FTE, 14 hours per week across Friday and one additional day) Duration: Until 30 July 2027 Level 6/7 | Salary: $96,898 - $119,986 p.a. pro rata plus 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be prompted to respond to a selection criteria questionnaire as part of the application process and indicate which position you are interested in. Please also attach your CV to your application. For further information about this position, please contact Courtney Faucett – People Advisory Support Manager at courtneyf@uow.edu.au Closing date: 8 November 2026, 11.59pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of al