      "description": "Conversion Specialist (Projects & Initiatives) - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Conversion Specialist (Projects & Initiatives) Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW), a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role As a Conversion Specialist (Projects & Initiatives), you will play a key role in supporting student recruitment outcomes by leading projects and initiatives across digital, physical and outbound touchpoints. Working at the intersection of communications, engagement and technology, you will help ensure prospective students receive accurate, timely and compelling information throughout their decision-making journey while contributing to the strategic objectives of the Student Growth and Engagement division. Key responsibilities: Lead the planning and delivery of projects that enhance the future student journey across digital, print and communication channels. Design and coordinate targeted conversion campaigns, including email, SMS and outbound engagement initiatives. Manage the end-to-end production of recruitment collateral including course guides, brochures and flyers. Build strong relationships with stakeholders across the University to gather requirements, coordinate content and deliver successful outcomes. Support technology enhancements and project delivery by translating operational needs into actionable solutions. About the Team The role sits within the Engagement and Conversion team in the Student Growth and Engagement division. The team supports student recruitment outcomes by developing and delivering strategies and initiatives that guide prospective students through critical decision-making and enrolment milestones. Working collaboratively across the University, the team delivers future student communications, recruitment collateral, operational processes and technology solutions that help prospective students make informed decisions about their future. What You'll Bring Relevant qualifications and/or experience in marketing, student recruitment, administration or a related field, supported by demonstrated project management experience. Experience coordinating campaigns, communications, publications or projects across multiple channels. Strong stakeholder engagement and relationship-building skills with the ability to influence and collaborate effectively. Experience using CRM platforms, marketing automation tools and content management systems. Excellent organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility. Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies. Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period. Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year. Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities. Role Details Employment type: Fixed-term | Full-time appointment to 24 December 2027 Level 6/7 | $96,898 - $119,986 plus 17% superannuation Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be requested to submit a CV and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Jeremy King, Senior Manager, Future Student Operations on +61 401 229 197. Closing Date: 8 November 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where 