      "description": "2  x Senior Business Analyst - Cyber and IDAM - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs 2  x Senior Business Analyst - Cyber and IDAM Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose‑driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. The University of Wollongong is undertaking a significant Cyber Security Uplift Program and is seeking experienced Senior Business Analysts to join our team. We have opportunities across two streams: Senior Business Analyst - Cyber Security Senior Business Analyst - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) These roles will play a key part in delivering strategic cyber security and identity initiatives that strengthen the University's security posture, improve governance and access controls, and support our broader digital transformation agenda. About the Roles Working closely with project managers, technical specialists, vendors, and business stakeholders, you will lead business analysis activities across complex cyber security projects. You will facilitate workshops, gather and document requirements, map business processes, support solution design, and ensure solutions meet business and security objectives. Depending on your area of expertise, you may contribute to initiatives involving: Cyber Security Cyber security control uplift and assurance activities Security assessments and remediation programs Process improvement aligned with frameworks such as NIST, ISO 27001 and Essential Eight Security solution implementation and testing Business readiness and stakeholder engagement activities Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Privileged Access Management (PAM) Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) User Access Certification (UAC) Single Sign-On (SSO) and Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) Identity governance and access management process improvement initiatives What You’ll Bring You are an experienced 