    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7094": {
      "title": "Student Communications and Knowledge Management Officer",
      "description": "Student Communications and Knowledge Management Officer - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Student Communications and Knowledge Management Officer Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose-driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role The Student Communications and Knowledge Management Officer plays an important role in enhancing the student experience by ensuring students can access clear, accurate and timely information throughout their university journey. Working across a range of digital communication and knowledge management channels, you will develop and maintain student-facing content, support communication campaigns, and help ensure frontline staff have access to the information they need to deliver exceptional service. This role contributes to a student-first approach by improving the quality, accessibility and effectiveness of communications and knowledge resources across the University. Key responsibilities: Create and maintain student-focused communications and knowledge content across digital platforms and channels. Develop clear, accessible and accurate information that supports both students and frontline staff. Collaborate with stakeholders across the University to gather, validate and manage content. Drive continuous improvement by identifying opportunities to enhance content quality, communication effectiveness and information discoverability. About the Team The role sits within the Student Frontline Service Unit in the Student Services Division, a team dedicated to delivering a seamless and supportive experience across the student lifecycle. The team oversees AskUOW, current student communications, the Student CRM and the University's knowledge management resources. Working closely with stakeholders across UOW, the team ensures students receive consistent, reliable and timely information to help them make informed decisions and succeed in their studies. What You'll Bring A bachelor's degree and relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Strong writing and editing skills, with the ability to create clear, accessible and student-centred content using plain English. Experience developing, publishing or maintaining content across digital communications, web or knowledge management platforms. Excellent stakeholder engagement skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with diverse subject matter experts. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining content accuracy and consistency. Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas-New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details 2 positions available 1 x Continuing, Full-time position, 1 x Continuing, Part-time position (29 hours per week) Level 5: $85,682 - $96,898 (pro rata for part time) plus 17% superannuation Location: Wollongong Campus Hybrid working Restrictions on leave during peak periods may apply. Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available. Position Description How to Apply Click on the 'Apply Now' button at the bottom of the advertisement. You'll be requested to submit a resume, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Alice Madden amadden@uow.edu.au Closing Date: Monday 2 November 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated. We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University's employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. UOW's Values in Action framework is built around four core values: Thrive Together, Pursue Excellence, Be Accountable, and Lead with Integrity, which guide how we work, collaborate and support our community. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7094 Job Category Marketing, Communications & Advancement Posting Date 10/19/2026, 07:37 PM Apply Before 11/02/2026, 04:55 AM Job Schedule Part time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs See More Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you 